# All phosphor-* extracted libraries ship as LGPL so third-party
# plugins / shells can link them without inheriting GPL — see CLAUDE.md
# for the per-tree license rules.
Files: phosphor/libs/phosphor-*/*
       phosphor-shell-libs/libs/phosphor-*/*
Copyright: 2026 fuddlesworth <fuddlesworth@users.noreply.github.com>
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later

# The LGPL tiers' own scaffolding, which the libs/phosphor-* globs above do not
# reach. These carry LGPL-2.1-or-later in their own SPDX headers, so the
# Files: * catch-all was asserting GPL-3 over them in the packaging metadata
# while the sources said otherwise.
#
# phosphor/data/schemas/*.json matters most here: it has no header (JSON has no
# comment syntax) but is RCC-embedded into PhosphorShaders, PhosphorZones and
# PhosphorAnimation, so declaring it GPL-3 asserts GPL over content compiled
# into LGPL shared libraries. That is the hazard CLAUDE.md names when it says
# never to "fix" a lib header to GPL-3, expressed in packaging metadata rather
# than in a header.
# cmake/ is MIXED, so its LGPL members are named one by one rather than
# globbed: format-qml.cmake, PhosphorCPack.cmake, PhosphorTranslations.cmake,
# post-install-sycoca.sh and uninstall.cmake.in are GPL-3 and must keep
# resolving to the catch-all.
Files: cmake/PhosphorLibTesting.cmake
       cmake/PhosphorTestIsolation.cmake
       cmake/PhosphorTier.cmake
       cmake/test-session-bus.conf
       phosphor/CMakeLists.txt
       phosphor/moon.yml
       phosphor/data/*
       phosphor-shell-libs/CMakeLists.txt
       phosphor-shell-libs/moon.yml
Copyright: 2026 fuddlesworth <fuddlesworth@users.noreply.github.com>
License: LGPL-2.1-or-later

